# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-2), L §2.3 `known = DAY`, §4.5: `known` is a day. A day known only to lie in a range is
# stated as the range's last day, with a note; `known window(a, b)` on a version or a row is refused by the grammar.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input x: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known window(2026-10-15, 2026-11-01)
  x = 1

ask q: x
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: expected a day, got window (m.tally:13)
